{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025120-positive-aspects-of-the-abyss-according-to-scelesti","id":1025120,"title":"Positive Aspects of the Abyss (According to Scelesti)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-01T11:04:37-08:00","id":1025120,"title":"Positive Aspects of the Abyss (According to Scelesti)","content":"Basically, I'm in the middle of writing my fanfic, and the ultimate mastermind of the plot is a Scelestus who fully believes in the whole Aswadim cosmology of the Tellurian being what happens when bits of the Abyss don't contradict, and create a fragile world-egg of Forms that barely fits together. As with the Dark Ones, he also believes this is a terrible thing that restricts Desire into unclean and torturous forms; the universe should have some Paradox injected into it, and turn the world into one defined mostly by wants, needs, and the constant chaotic interplay of laws born of them.<br /> <br /> Thing is though, he doesn't expect people to just accept it; even he still understands some wants are just plain wrong and should be overwritten by the collective will of others who aren't fans of being victimized by huge bullies. So he has a list of examples to cite when people argue with him that his dream would be a nightmare of reality-scale violence. The most pertinent one is that he sincerely believes that changelings can only escape their Durances because the Abyss corrupted Fairie at some point; the laws of the place would have it that humans would be brainwashed slaves forever, but thanks to the Void, a Kept can forcefully etch &quot;I have agency&quot; into Fate itself and become something fundamentally both fae and human, sane and mad, and neither. In fact, he almost worships them, as the truest children of Paradox.<br /> <br /> <b>That set me off thinking about other arguments Scelesti who still make a show of understanding humanity attempting to convince the world of the rightness of their cause would come up with. Any other ideas (strange or sympathetic)?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T11:21:24-08:00","id":1025121,"title":"","content":"The Fangs of Mara use the Abyss to fight Abyssal creatures. They might argue one can't truly fight an opponent without knowing it.<br /> <br /> Some could point to the Abyss as a natural aspect of the world, and it's corrupting influence only a result of the Fallen World's methods of imprisonment, or worse, backlash as a result of millenia of demonizing and rejecting it.<br /> <br /> They might refer to the Abyssal shard within everyone as evidence that it's an important aspect of life. As a source of things that cannot be, perhaps it allows for ideas and events to bring in that allow for deviations from the Exarch's victory. If the Exarchs have truly won, who's to say it's the mythical Oracles that offer mages their free will, and not the Abyss that was part of them as a human and traveled through during their Awakening?<br /> <br /> A lot of the example Scelesti seem to point at 'wrongness' of the world and attempt to use the Scelestus route to create a new world and fix it.<br /> <br /> It is, of course, infinite and within it one might potentially find anything, including improvements one could apply to the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T23:23:43-08:00","id":1025319,"title":"","content":"As the example Aswadim says in Imperial Mysteries, sometimes the comforting Lie is better than the cold Truth.<br /> <br /> The Just World hypothesis is false. All claims to the contrary, the same. Certainly, some will try to argue that the world could <i>be</i> just, if people worked towards it or such-and-such were changed, but that ostensibly means the world <i>isn't</i> just now, and that any such possible future state where it might be would only be temporary and generalized, not specific.<br /> <br /> This is not the fault of the Abyss. Much as people might like to believe otherwise, there is nothing unnatural about pain or agony or misery or death. Bubonic plague is as natural as the air we breathe. Even if one were to assume an idealized universe where all people are Awakened and fully empowered to live as they see fit, no one person would ever be free from the cruelties and vagaries of life. The Awakened prove as much, eternally vexed as they are by problem and worry. Being the world's greatest healer only seems to encourage further challenges; constantly confronted by magical ailments, for a healer is defined by the need to heal.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be nice if that were not the case? Wouldn't it be wonderful if the physician could exist in the absence of disease? Where the world was not defined by contexts, and so good could exist without evil?<br /> <br /> If the universe is harsh and cruel, and demands you suffer for the mere sin of existing, perhaps it's time to find a better universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T23:36:15-08:00","id":1025321,"title":"","content":"I had a street-level Scelestus in my game whose argument to the PCs was just selfish apathy. (they didn't go for it.)<br /> <br /> Carrot: the Abyss is an easy source of power, either by befouling your spells or summoning entities outright. Most Gulmoth don't bother with wheedling or driving a hard bargain for their services, because if they're being summoned at all, they've already got what they want. Drawing on the Abyss makes you better at magic and pursuing your Obsessions, and gives you a tool other mages can't counter. It's fun to piss off the orthodox mages who thought they could tell you what to do by doing the impossible things they're afraid of. Also, it feels good.<br /> <br /> Stick: mages freaking out about the abstract cosmological consequences about &quot;fraying the Tapestry&quot; or whatever are like those people who try to explain why you personally shouldn't shoplift a stick of gum by going back to like, John Locke and the social contract and shit. Do you honestly think you're important enough on a cosmic scale to break the world? Get real. It's like global warming: yeah, it's probably bad (if it's even real), but it's not like anyone is going to slow it down by abstaining from driving. If anything really majorly dangerous happened to reality (which, again, would not be your fault in any meaningful way), the Exarchs or the Archmages or the God-Machine or Jesus or <i>someone</i> would step in.<br /> <br /> Only a sucker turns down free money because they're afraid of getting caught. You're not a sucker, are you?<br /> <br /> e: you and I both know you're not going to get far in life playing by the rules. You think all those fat cats on Wall Street got their billions or the new guy got elected because they stayed on the straight and narrow, or because they knew how the game <i>really</i> worked? The Hierarch/Councilor/Minister got where they are by drawing on the Abyss, I guarantee you. <i>Everyone</i> does it sometime- everyone who actually gets what they want. You're hobbling yourself right out of the gate if you don't befoul your spells or let an Acamoth dreamride you, too. Why don't you at least try it, one time? Then you can make an informed decision, and that puts you head and shoulders above those dweebs who blindly believe what their bosses tell them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-02-2017, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T23:52:03-08:00","id":1025323,"title":"","content":"Now, I've done some bad things - really bad. I have the feeling I'm not the only one. But I just couldn't <i>live</i> with it, ya know?<br /> <br /> So I tried to kill myself. It seemed obvious, at the time - of course, I Awakened in Stygia. And then death stopped looking like a way out, or a punishment. I realized then that reality, both Fallen and Supernal, <i>refuses</i> non-existence. Everything's just one big cycle, and I can't cut away the things I've done - it's impossible.<br /> <br /> Well <i>fuck</i> that! Things in the Abyss <i>aren't</i>, and never were. So if I can just feed my past to that - feed <i>me</i> to <i>it</i>...<br /> <br /> There won't be anything to be sorry about anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}